"""Uncle, part B: Personality (official descriptions, traits, In his own words, Names, Appearance),
Skills/gameplay/weapons/horses, Relationships (19 Oct 2026).

Sources (register): Rockstar character description of 6 Sep 2018 (English text as reprinted by The
Hollywood Reporter / Heat Vision, Sep 2018, saved in ../charles/fc/thr_descriptions.txt; French text
from rockstargames.com/reddeadredemption2/fr/features/vanderlindegang, as quoted by the French Red
Dead Wiki page "L'Oncle", saved in uncle/fr.txt); a character biography page from an official guide
(wiki file UncleBio.jpg, captioned "Biography in RDR 2", downloaded to uncle/fc/UncleBio.png and read:
text quoted verbatim, edition not identified); Red Dead Wiki EN "Uncle" (infobox, quote box,
Personality, Appearance, Quotes, Trivia, Gallery captions); FR "L'Oncle"; wiki pages "Camp Events"
(chapters 2, 3, 4), "Go Rustling (Uncle)", "High and Low Finance", "An Honest Mistake", "Old Friends",
"Eastward Bound", "A New Jerusalem", "The Tool Box", "A New Future Imagined", "Home of the Gentry?",
"By Sweat and Toil", "A Continual Feast". Transcripts: Polite Society, Valentine Style; The Aftermath
of Genesis; Eastward Bound; Old Friends; Home Improvement for Beginners; American Venom (opening);
The Outlaw's Return; By Sweat and Toil; A Continual Feast; Wolves, Dogs and Sons; Old Friends, New
Problems; Spare the Love, Spoil the Child; The Last Enemy That Shall Be Destroyed. Fact-checked fiches
reused as is: arthur_D (Uncle entry), dutch_C, micah_B, hosea_B, charles_B, bill_B, javier_B, sadie_B,
abigail_B, jack_B, john_D.

Ownership (FIX_RULES): official descriptions (Rockstar 2018 EN+FR, guide biography page, the wiki's
Complete Official Guide quote), names (Uncle, l'Oncle, nephew, Old Uncle, old man, one-shot kid, camp
rat), appearance (incl. 1911 glove and beard stain), skills, gameplay (companion activities, camp
availability, random encounters, Eagle Eye, mission strand, Beecher's Hope routines incl. the spot
where he dies in 1911), weapons and horses, and all camp scenes live HERE. Each camp scene sits in ONE
relationship entry (cow piss tease, "outlive them all", leave/dying chats -> Arthur; food
line, Mac Callander, cheering-up attempt -> Bill; Hosea's stories, Timbuktu, running women -> Hosea;
silence -> Charles; drink after the camp box -> Javier; harassment
and "parasite" -> Micah; mooning -> Swanson; evening in town -> Susan; Ohio/Cornwall -> Trelawny;
sea, orphan story, Congo, Brazil -> Pearson; American king talk -> Dutch). Songs are listed once, in
Skills. Narrative events (Blackwater, Colter, Valentine trip as a story, An Honest Mistake, Go Rustling
as a story, Molly at Beaver Hollow, departure, 1907 reunion and building, Skinner kidnapping, wedding,
1911 return, the two ranch missions as stories, the final attack, burial, Undead Nightmare) live in
part A; relationship entries refer to them in a short clause.
Lines quoted in this part (parts A and C must NOT repeat them): Rockstar EN/FR descriptions, the
guide page and the Complete Official Guide fragment "not exactly the most productive"; "It's like
people call me lazy..."; "I was thinking." / "Does it pay well?" / "Eventually."; "Oh, I got lumbago,
it's very serious!"; "L-lumbago! It's really serious, it can be deadly."; "I'm real sick, John.
Lumbago..." (wiki quote list, "Home of the Gentry?"); "Come on, I'm getting old..." / "You've been
taking things easy for forty years."; "Nothing worse for an old man than sleeping in the warm
afternoon sun."; "couldn't hit the ground with your hat in three throws"; "A drop of whiskey for a
start."; "one-shot kid"; "Trust Old Uncle."; John's "He's probably lots of people's father, though."
and "Folks always did..." (order of the transcript: "really your uncle?" first); "Get up, old man." /
"What are you looking at, old man?"; "camp rat" (Names ONLY); "Uncle, Reverend Swanson... no more
passengers." (Dutch entry; A paraphrases without quotes); "repulsive old lizard" / "Lizards have
hearts!"; "Or is that Uncle?"; "'Bout the one thing Uncle didn't manage to have stolen while we was
gone."; "Uncle warned me about women like you." (C Trivia must not repeat it).
Moved out after fact-check (19 Oct 2026): "Is that any way to greet an old friend?" and "He loves me
really..." (C Quotes only; Arthur entry points there); "I love it, I truly love it." (C Quotes; Jack
entry paraphrases); "away with you, you no good parasite... you cook." (A Biography); "Charles, make
him work. Whip him..." (John's line, A Biography); "I tried to stop him." and "Uncle told me about
it." (paraphrased); "good friends one day" after High and Low Finance (A Biography only); the
introduction of Abigail around 1894 (A); Go Rustling sale and split, High and Low Finance dynamite,
Valentine directions, pre-cut house details and lumbago in "A New Jerusalem", rancher claim (A).
Jack's prank on a sleeping Uncle: removed (not found in the saved French wiki page fr.txt).
Coverage adds: thief among former occupations (wiki infobox, attributed); blue bandana vs black ones
(wiki trivia, attributed).

WIKI-ONLY (kept, attributed): the Complete Official Guide fragment (quoted); thief as former occupation
(infobox); blue bandana (trivia); "nephew" camp line
(footnote, paraphrased); grudge against the British (trivia, paraphrased); Englishmen bar story
(trivia, via jack_B); "I'll outlive you all" (trivia, paraphrased); High and Low Finance lookout (character trivia);
American king talk with Dutch (character page, YouTube footnote, paraphrased); Javier questioning his
loyalty (via javier_B); "looked out for you" line in "A Continual Feast" (footnote only: NOT in the
saved transcript, attributed as abigail_B does); Arthur's "leave"/"dying" chats and "luckiest man
alive" (Arthur_Morgan/Relationships page); "Your Misery"
(Dutch infobox); Beecher's Hope routines (trivia, gallery captions); RDR1 tasks (trivia); weapons,
horses (infobox, trivia, gallery).

Excluded: "reformed petty thief", "seeking redemption", "more intelligent and shrewd than he may
appear", "strong sense of loyalty", "caring side" (wiki interpretation); rhinophyma / "whiskey nose"
(wiki reading of the model); "appears to have shrunk" (wiki guess); "a refusal to give his real name"
(no line found where he refuses: only that the name is never given); real name, birth year, age
(never given; birth range belongs to part A if kept); wife count and Ohio birth (part A Origins);
Africa/Congo god story details (part A Origins; only the Pearson camp scene is here); outfit
catalogue (SPEC); hat shot off, unlootable corpse, killable with dynamite, Ross outfit, multiplayer,
Lookin' for Some Posse, Wishbone (part C/D); actors (part D); GamesRadar "addicts" (part D Reception);
Strauss, Lenny, Bonnie, Fordham, Landon Ricketts (no Uncle-specific story fact found; Ricketts only
shares the Myths and Mavericks multiplayer pack, part C); Sean (only shared songs, listed in Skills);
Rains Fall (no shared scene found, slug not live); Undead Nightmare in relationship entries (non-canon,
part A).
"""

def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- PERSONALITY
BLOCKS_PERSONALITY = [
    {"h3": two("Personality", "Personnalité")},
    {"p": two(
        "Rockstar's character description, published on September 6, 2018, reads: \"A hanger-on and good-time guy, Uncle is always around when the whiskey is open and never around when there's any work to be done. If he wasn't so entertaining, Dutch would have cut him loose years ago.\" A character biography page from an official guide, reproduced on the Red Dead Wiki, opens with almost the same sentence and continues: \"Nobody is quite sure how old he is, how he's still alive, or if he's actually anybody's uncle. He's lived a colorful life that gets more vibrant with every story he tells. He claims to have had many wives and to have traveled to every corner of the globe; he also asserts he has terminal lumbago.\" In the guide's version, it is the gang, not Dutch, that would have cut him loose. The Red Dead Wiki also quotes The Complete Official Guide, which calls him \"not exactly the most productive\" member of the gang, a whoremonger and a drunkard. The wiki's infobox lists thief among his former occupations.",
        "La description officielle publiée par Rockstar le 6 septembre 2018 (version française) : « Opportuniste et bon vivant, l'Oncle est toujours partant pour une bonne bouteille de whisky, mais disparaît mystérieusement chaque fois qu'il y a des choses à faire. Dutch s'en serait déjà séparé il y a des années s'il n'était pas si amusant. » Une page de biographie tirée d'un guide officiel, reproduite sur le Red Dead Wiki, reprend presque mot pour mot la première phrase, puis ajoute : \"Nobody is quite sure how old he is, how he's still alive, or if he's actually anybody's uncle. He's lived a colorful life that gets more vibrant with every story he tells. He claims to have had many wives and to have traveled to every corner of the globe; he also asserts he has terminal lumbago.\" (personne ne sait vraiment quel âge il a, comment il est encore en vie, ni s'il est l'oncle de qui que ce soit ; sa vie haute en couleur gagne en éclat à chaque histoire qu'il raconte ; il prétend avoir eu de nombreuses épouses et parcouru le monde entier, et affirme souffrir d'un lumbago en phase terminale). Dans la version du guide, c'est le gang, et non Dutch, qui s'en serait séparé. Le Red Dead Wiki cite aussi The Complete Official Guide, qui le juge \"not exactly the most productive\" (pas vraiment le plus productif) des membres du gang et le décrit comme un coureur de bordels et un ivrogne. L'encadré du wiki range le vol parmi ses anciennes occupations.")},
    {"p": two(
        "His excuse for avoiding work is lumbago, a pain in the lower back that is not a fatal condition; he presents it as a deadly illness, in 1899 and again in 1907. Arthur, John, Abigail, Dutch and Micah all reproach him for his idleness at some point (see Relationships). John sums up his routine in 1911, in \"A Continual Feast\": asleep half the day, and the other half so drunk that he \"couldn't hit the ground with your hat in three throws\". Whiskey comes first on his shopping list in Valentine: \"A drop of whiskey for a start.\" He is also a teller of tales whose stories the games never confirm (see Origins).",
        "Pour échapper au travail, il invoque son lumbago, une douleur du bas du dos qui n'a rien de mortel ; il le présente comme une maladie fatale, en 1899 comme en 1907. Arthur, John, Abigail, Dutch et Micah lui reprochent tous sa paresse à un moment ou à un autre (voir les relations). En 1911, dans \"A Continual Feast\", John résume ses journées : la moitié du temps endormi, l'autre moitié trop soûl pour \"hit the ground with your hat in three throws\" (toucher le sol avec son chapeau en trois essais). À Valentine, le whisky arrive en tête de sa liste de courses : \"A drop of whiskey for a start\" (une goutte de whisky, pour commencer). C'est aussi un conteur, dont les jeux ne confirment jamais les récits (voir Origines).")},
    {"p": two(
        "At Horseshoe Overlook he tries more than once to lift the camp's mood, with his father's lesson about living in the present (see Origins) or by calling for a song (see Bill Williamson). A newspaper tells him that the United States is going to war in the Philippines; he says he neither understands the war nor approves of it. At the Clemens Point campfire he says the country gets worse every year, and names wars, the legacy of slavery and greed. According to the Red Dead Wiki, he also has a grudge against the British: he calls their voices silly and the people stuffed-shirted windbags.",
        "À Horseshoe Overlook, il tente plus d'une fois de remonter le moral du camp, avec la leçon de son père sur le présent (voir Origines) ou en réclamant une chanson (voir Bill Williamson). Le journal lui apprend que les États-Unis partent en guerre aux Philippines : il dit ne pas comprendre cette guerre et ne pas l'approuver. Au coin du feu de Clemens Point, il juge que le pays empire d'année en année, à cause des guerres, de l'héritage de l'esclavage et de la cupidité. D'après le Red Dead Wiki, il en veut aussi aux Britanniques, dont il trouve la voix ridicule et qu'il traite de baudruches guindées.")},
    {"h4": two("In his own words", "Dans ses propres mots")},
    {"p": two(
        "The Red Dead Wiki opens its page on him with this line: \"It's like people call me lazy. I'm not lazy, just don't like working. There's a difference.\" In \"Polite Society, Valentine Style\" (1899), Arthur finds him asleep at camp. \"I was thinking,\" Uncle says. Arthur: \"Does it pay well?\" Uncle: \"Eventually.\" On the road, when Tilly asks who will fetch a stranded driver's horse: \"Oh, I got lumbago, it's very serious!\" If Arthur rides on, Karen asks him why he did not help, and he answers: \"L-lumbago! It's really serious, it can be deadly.\" In 1907 the wiki's quote list gives his version to John, in \"Home of the Gentry?\": \"I'm real sick, John. Lumbago. It's a slow and painful death, my brother.\"",
        "Le Red Dead Wiki ouvre sa page sur cette réplique : \"It's like people call me lazy. I'm not lazy, just don't like working. There's a difference.\" (on me traite de paresseux ; je ne suis pas paresseux, simplement je n'aime pas travailler ; ce n'est pas pareil). Dans \"Polite Society, Valentine Style\" (1899), Arthur le trouve endormi au camp. \"I was thinking\" (je réfléchissais), se défend Uncle. Arthur : \"Does it pay well?\" (ça paie bien ?). Uncle : \"Eventually\" (à terme). En route, quand Tilly demande qui ira chercher le cheval d'un cocher en difficulté : \"Oh, I got lumbago, it's very serious!\" (j'ai un lumbago, c'est très grave !). Si Arthur passe son chemin, Karen lui demande pourquoi il n'a pas aidé, et il répond : \"L-lumbago! It's really serious, it can be deadly.\" (le lumbago ! c'est vraiment grave, ça peut être mortel). En 1907, la liste de citations du wiki donne sa version pour John, dans \"Home of the Gentry?\" : \"I'm real sick, John. Lumbago. It's a slow and painful death, my brother.\" (je suis très malade, John ; un lumbago ; c'est une mort lente et douloureuse, mon frère).")},
    {"p": two(
        "In 1911, when John wakes him in \"By Sweat and Toil\": \"Nothing worse for an old man than sleeping in the warm afternoon sun.\" Riding out in \"A Continual Feast\", he pleads his age: \"Come on, I'm getting old. I gotta start taking things easy.\" John answers: \"You've been taking things easy for forty years.\"",
        "En 1911, quand John le réveille dans \"By Sweat and Toil\" : \"Nothing worse for an old man than sleeping in the warm afternoon sun.\" (rien de pire pour un vieil homme que de dormir sous le chaud soleil de l'après-midi). En route, dans \"A Continual Feast\", il invoque son âge : \"Come on, I'm getting old. I gotta start taking things easy.\" (allons, je me fais vieux, il faut que je commence à me ménager). John lui répond : \"You've been taking things easy for forty years.\" (ça fait quarante ans que tu te ménages).")},
    {"h4": two("Names", "Noms")},
    {"p": two(
        "Neither game gives his real name. In \"Wolves, Dogs and Sons\" (1911), Jack first asks whether Uncle is really John's uncle. John says he sincerely hopes not, and adds: \"He's probably lots of people's father, though.\" Jack then asks why they call him Uncle, and John answers: \"Folks always did. Probably 'cause he's always been older than everybody else.\" According to the Red Dead Wiki, Uncle says in a camp scene that before people called him Uncle, as a little boy, they called him nephew. Rockstar's French text and the French Red Dead Wiki call him l'Oncle.",
        "Aucun des deux jeux ne donne son vrai nom. Dans \"Wolves, Dogs and Sons\" (1911), Jack demande d'abord si Uncle est vraiment l'oncle de son père. John espère sincèrement que non, et ajoute : \"He's probably lots of people's father, though.\" (en revanche, il est sans doute le père de pas mal de gens). Jack veut alors savoir pourquoi on l'appelle Uncle, et John répond : \"Folks always did. Probably 'cause he's always been older than everybody else.\" (tout le monde l'a toujours appelé comme ça ; sans doute parce qu'il a toujours été plus vieux que les autres). D'après le Red Dead Wiki, Uncle raconte dans une scène de camp qu'avant qu'on l'appelle l'oncle, quand il était petit, on l'appelait le neveu. Le texte français de Rockstar et le Red Dead Wiki français le nomment l'Oncle.")},
    {"p": two(
        "In Valentine he tells Arthur that in his youth he \"used to be known as the 'one-shot kid'\"; Arthur says he will not ask why. He speaks of himself in the third person as Old Uncle (\"Trust Old Uncle.\"). John calls him old man throughout Red Dead Redemption (\"Get up, old man.\", \"What are you looking at, old man?\"), and Arthur greets him at Colter as the \"camp rat\". The Red Dead Wiki lists Uncle, Old Man and One-Shot Kid as his names, the last marked as self-claimed and unconfirmed.",
        "À Valentine, il confie à Arthur que dans sa jeunesse il \"used to be known as the 'one-shot kid'\" (était connu comme le gamin qui tire une seule fois) ; Arthur préfère ne pas demander pourquoi. Il parle de lui-même à la troisième personne en Old Uncle (\"Trust Old Uncle\", fais confiance au vieil oncle). Dans Red Dead Redemption, John l'appelle sans cesse le vieux (\"Get up, old man.\", debout, le vieux ; \"What are you looking at, old man?\", qu'est-ce que tu regardes, le vieux ?), et à Colter Arthur l'accueille en \"camp rat\" (rat du camp). Le Red Dead Wiki retient Uncle, Old Man et One-Shot Kid, ce dernier étant signalé comme revendiqué par lui seul et non confirmé.")},
    {"h4": two("Appearance", "Apparence")},
    {"p": two(
        "The guide's portrait shows a heavy-set man, bald on top, with gray hair at the sides, a full gray beard and a red face, wearing a blue bandana, suspenders and worn trousers, a bottle of whiskey in his hand. The Red Dead Wiki notes that the bandana sets him apart: most gang members wear black ones, and only Dutch and Lenny also wear another color. In all three periods he keeps a brown hat and a gun belt with a single holster, according to the Red Dead Wiki. In 1911 he wears a single beige glove on his right hand, and his beard has a yellow-brown stain that is absent from Red Dead Redemption 2.",
        "Le portrait du guide montre un homme corpulent, chauve sur le dessus du crâne, les tempes grises, une grande barbe grise et le visage rougeaud, avec un bandana bleu, des bretelles et un pantalon usé, une bouteille de whisky à la main. Le Red Dead Wiki relève que ce bandana le distingue : la plupart des membres du gang en portent un noir, et seuls Dutch et Lenny en ont aussi d'une autre couleur. À toutes les époques, il garde un chapeau brun et un ceinturon à un seul étui, selon le Red Dead Wiki. En 1911, il porte un unique gant beige à la main droite, et sa barbe a une tache jaunâtre qui n'existe pas dans Red Dead Redemption 2.")},
]

